Aim
To write a Python program using NumPy and Pandas to perform basic mathematical operations on an array and display and analyse student data using a DataFrame.

Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Import the NumPy and Pandas libraries.
3. Create a NumPy array containing five elements.
4. Display the array.
5. Calculate and display the sum, mean, maximum and minimum values of the array.
6. Create a dictionary containing student names, ages and marks.
7. Convert the dictionary into a Pandas DataFrame.
8. Display the DataFrame.
9. Display the student names.
10. Calculate and display the average marks.
11. Stop the program.

Code:

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
# NumPy implementation
arr = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50])
print("NumPy Array:", arr)
print("Sum:", np.sum(arr))
print("Mean:", np.mean(arr))
print("Maximum:", np.max(arr))
print("Minimum:", np.min(arr))
# Pandas implementation
data = {
    "Name": ["Siya", "Riya", "Priya"],
    "Age": [20, 21, 19],
    "Marks": [90, 85, 95]
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
print("\nPandas DataFrame:")
print(df)
print("\nStudent Names:")
print(df["Name"])
print("\nAverage Marks:")
print(df["Marks"].mean())

